  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evidence-Based Multisectoral Humanitarian Response to the Most Vulnerable Populations in the Earthquake Affected Provinces in T&#xfc;rkiye</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After more than a year since the twin earthquakes that hit T&#xfc;rkiye, as per the latest Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) post-earthquake neighbourhood and site mapping data as of October 2023; 761,054 individuals remained displaced and approximately 355,000 individuals remained in informal settlements across most affected four provinces and three districts covered in Gaziantep and Osmaniye. 
 
This Action will promote the well-being of those most vulnerable populations, including those affected by the earthquake through coordinated, evidence-based and multisectoral assistance. In coordination with the central and local governmental authorities, humanitarian partners, Temporary Settlement Support (TSS) Sector and Area-Based Coordination (ABC) hubs, IOM is providing i) Shelter and Settlement, ii) Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services, and iii) Multipurpose Cash Assistance (MPCA) in the formal and informal sites in which the high number of refuges remain in need of assistance. This Action will also contribute to support an evidence-based response and prioritisation of all humanitarian and development actors given DTM&#x2019;s wider role as a common data source for all actors operating in T&#xfc;rkiye, across different response frameworks.</narrative>
  </description>
